findings.comment:
Observed the following single-use containers stored upright without protection so that their food-contact surfaces are exposed to potential contamination:
(i) single-use cardboard containers stored on an upper shelf without any protection from above;
(ii) single-service sauce containers stored in a larger open container;
(Iiii) larger rounded plastic containers and their lids stored on an upper shelf.
CORRECTED: PIC was notified and had staff invert containers or moved them underneath a closed shelf to ensure the food-contact surfaces are protected.
